<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN CAR REGISTRATIONS DOWN 5.2% IN YR TO APRIL.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN CAR REGISTRATIONS DOWN 5.2% IN YR TO APRIL.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian new car registrations</p>
<p>fell 5.2 percent in the year to April compared with the same</p>
<p>year ago period, according to figures from the Belgian National</p>
<p>Statistics Institute.</p>
<p>Registrations were up 1.9 percent in April from April</p>
<p>1996.</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CAR REGISTRATIONS April 97	 April 96</p>
<p>    Month			   40,771	  39,997</p>
<p>    Cumulative Jan-April     163,689	 172,618</p>
<p>April registrations by manufacturer and market share for</p>
<p>those above three percent versus 1996 period.</p>
<p> VW	 8,379 (20.6 pct)  vs   7,126   (17.8 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot 5,945 (14.6 pct)  vs   5,678   (14.2 pct)</p>
<p> GM	   4,605 (11.3 pct)  vs   4,329   (10.8 pct)</p>
<p> Renault 4,473 (11.0 pct)  vs   4,969   (12.4 pct)</p>
<p> Ford Motor  3,447  (8.5 pct)  vs   4,923   (12.3 pct)</p>
<p> BMW Group 2,093  (5.1 pct)  vs   2,087    (5.2 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota   1,945  (4.8 pct)  vs   1,749    (4.4 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat     1,868  (4.6 pct)  vs   1,824    (4.6 pct)</p>
<p> Mercedes 1,410  (3.5 pct)  vs   1,055    (2.6 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan   1,278  (3.1 pct)  vs   1,022    (2.6 pct)</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
